कतक m. the Kataka tree;
 n. the nut of it (used for
clearing water).

कातर a. cowardly, timid, shy, afraid of (loc., inf., or
—˚);
 abstr. ˚ता f., ˚त्व n.

कत्थ् कत्थते (कत्थ˚ति) boast, praise, flatter;
abuse, blame. — वि boast or brag of (instr.), praise, extol;
 degrade,
humble (also C.).

कातन्त्र n. title of a grammar;
 m. pl. the followers of
the Katantra grammar.

कात्यायनीय m. pl. the followers of Kātyāyana;
 n. T.
of sev. works.
